# lector-config write-method names that are also common method names (`HashMap::remove`,
# `Vec::clear`, ...). The `purity` rule flags them in lector-review only when the receiver's name
# contains `store`, `config`, `settings`, `session`, `recent` or `backend`. One name per line,
# each with a reason.

# Also `HashMap::remove` / `Vec::remove` (RecentProjects::remove writes recents.json).
remove
# Also `Vec::clear` / `HashSet::clear` style setters; ReviewBackend::set writes a viewed mark.
set
# Also `Vec::insert` / `HashMap::insert`.
insert
# Also `Vec::clear` and `HashMap::clear`.
clear
# Also `HashSet::add`-style builders.
add
# Also `Vec::push`-style recorders (RecentProjects::record).
record
